course: dictionary
lesson: 4544
title: Heartfelt feelings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Heartfelt means deeply and sincerely felt, coming truly from the heart. When someone gives you heartfelt thanks, they really mean every word. Heart and felt are two clues hidden in the word.
explain: Look at the words around it. «proBAch means forgive me, a heartfelt sorry after a real quarrel; it is stronger than vybaCHAI.» The clues are forgive me and real quarrel. A heartfelt sorry is not a quick word said to end the fuss. It comes from deep down, so it is stronger than an ordinary sorry.
explain: Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence. Swap in deeply and truly meant and check that the sentence still makes sense. If it does, you have found the meaning.
fact: Heartfelt means deeply and sincerely felt, coming truly from the heart.
fact: We give heartfelt thanks, heartfelt apologies and heartfelt wishes when we really mean them.
fact: Heartfelt condolences are said when someone has died, to show you feel their loss deeply.
fact: In a story, a heartfelt speech or letter shows that the character is honest and moved.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «She sent me a heartfelt thank you for helping her.» What does heartfelt mean here? | Written in pencil | Quick and careless, said without thinking | Very loud and noisy | *Deeply and truly meant, from the heart
exercise: Nadia says heartfelt is just another word for happy. Why is that not quite right? | It is a longer word | *It means sincerely felt, which goes deeper than just being happy | It means sad and tired | It means exactly the same as happy, so there is no difference at all
exercise: «The letter was full of heartfelt wishes for her recovery.» Find and copy the word that describes the wishes. | full | recovery | *heartfelt | letter
test: «The crowd gave a heartfelt cheer when the team won.» What does heartfelt show about the cheer? | The crowd was asleep | *The cheer was real and came from deep feeling | The cheer was fake and forced | Nobody was there to cheer
test: Which phrase is said when someone has died? | *Heartfelt condolences | Heartfelt wishes | Heartfelt speech | Heartfelt thanks
exam: Which sentence shows a heartfelt feeling? | I said sorry by accident while reading | *He wrote a letter saying sorry from the bottom of his heart | "Ugh, fine, sorry," said with a sigh | Sorry is a word with four letters
